Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 02:57:01 -0500
Subject: fix(translate): no request for the language list without an API key
 (S-556)

Without an API key no page is ever offered for translation
(TranslateManager::IsAvailable), yet TranslateLanguageList asked
translate.googleapis.com for its list whenever Settings' Languages section
or the live-caption translation menu listed languages, whatever Translate's
setting said (GitHub issue 133). The request is not made without a key; the
built-in list answers. Upstream's GetSupportedLanguagesFetch already skips
without one, and NoFetchWithoutAnApiKey skips with one.

Test: TranslateLanguageListTest.NoFetchWithoutAnApiKey (components_unittests).

Why: Stedding promises no request it has no use for (docs/PRIVACY.md), and
with no API key Translate's list is never used.
Removable when: Stedding ships an API key and offers translation, or
upstream stops asking for the list without one.
